  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 7 items closed, including one that arrived while I worked. Three results that arrived during the work changed three decisions; I corrected each one.\n\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: first renewed for 90 days and ordered a BMP, because the August potassium of 5.9 was hemolyzed and doesn't count. Then a valid outside BMP arrived (drawn 10/20, K 5.8), so I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001). Urgent PCP review task task-t0014 (focus mr-00283). The repeat BMP order sr-t0002 stays in place. Patient sent a correction.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030):\n  - Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58 even after the lab correction; HbA1c was 7.1% on 8/19 (outside lab). All 3 metformin messages (patient + 2 pharmacy) were treated as one request with one order.\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: first renewed. Then the 10/06 creatinine was corrected to 1.49, 35.5% above the 1.10 before the September dose increase. The protocol handles that like a high potassium, so I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003). Urgent PCP review task task-t0015 (focus mr-00295). Patient sent a correction.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  - Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days (mr-t0007). eGFR 92 and HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28; the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error.\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: first a 30-day supply plus a BMP order, since no BMP was within 12 months. Then a BMP drawn 10/22 arrived (K 4.6), so I renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0013, replacing mr-t0005). Patient updated.\n  - The BMP order sr-t0006 is now redundant and I have no way to cancel a lab order, so task-t0016 asks for it to be cancelled.\n\nMr. Odum's and Mr. Price's lisinopril orders now show as stopped (my renewals replaced them, then I cancelled the renewals). Neither has an active lisinopril order until you decide; Mr. Price says his supply has already run out.\n\nEach patient got replies, and each chart has a telephone note citing RBC-RX-05. The three new results-queue items that triggered these changes (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) are still open in your results queue for you; I only cleared the messages queue.",
